RC - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

Background services ("daemons"). A service is
/etc/rc.d/NAME.lua defining start() and optionally
stop(), status() and other commands. /etc/rc.cfg
lists services started at boot (enabled = {...})
and settings per service (NAME = {...}, visible to
the script as the global args). The rc program
wraps this library.

rc.run(name, command, ...) -> ok, result

Runs a command of a service: "start", "stop",
"restart", "status" or any function the script
defines. Loads the script on first use. Returns
nil, reason on failure.

rc.runCommand(name, command, ...) -> ok, result

The OpenOS name for rc.run.

rc.allRunCommand(command, ...) -> table

Runs a command on every running service: {[name] =
{ok, result}}.

rc.load(name) -> environment

Loads a service script and returns its environment
(the table with its functions).

rc.list() -> table

Names of all services in /etc/rc.d.

rc.isEnabled(name) -> boolean

Whether a service starts at boot.

rc.enable(name) / rc.disable(name)

Adds a service to / removes it from the boot list
in /etc/rc.cfg.

rc.startEnabled()

Starts every enabled service. The OS calls this at
boot.

rc.loaded, rc.running

Tables of loaded service environments and of
running services ({[name] = true}).
